---
import BlogPost from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Is there a free online speed reader that does not require signup?',
    a: 'Yes. BriskRead runs in the browser at briskread.com with no account required for RSVP, Focus, Bionic, paste, PDF/EPUB, and optional Audio Sync. Every feature is free; an optional account only adds multi-device sync.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is BriskRead really free?',
    a: 'Yes — all of it. Ads support the service; there are no paid tiers.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the best free RSVP speed reader for PDFs?',
    a: 'Choose a tool that parses PDFs locally in the browser, supports adjustable WPM, and lets you slow down for dense pages. BriskRead does local PDF/EPUB parsing, Flash RSVP with ORP highlight, and optional TTS Audio Sync.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does a free online speed reader upload my files?',
    a: 'It depends on the product. BriskRead processes paste, PDF, EPUB, and OCR client-side so documents are not stored on BriskRead servers by default. Optional URL extract and AI features call third parties as described in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need Chrome?',
    a: 'Any modern browser works for the website. The <a href="/extension">Chrome extension</a> adds page capture and in-tab reading.',
  },
];
---

<BlogPost slug="free-online-speed-reader" faqs={faqs} related={['rsvp-reading-explained', 'speed-read-pdf-online', 'how-to-speed-read-online']}>
  <div class="tldr" role="note" aria-label="Key takeaways">
    <p class="tldr-label">TL;DR</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>BriskRead</strong> is a free browser speed reader — open <a href="/">briskread.com</a>, paste or upload, start reading.</li>
      <li>No account needed for any mode: Flash RSVP, Phrase, Focus, Flow, Bionic, Page, and optional Audio Sync.</li>
      <li>PDFs and EPUBs parse <strong>locally</strong> in your browser by default.</li>
      <li>Unlimited document length — no caps, no paywalls. Supported by ads.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p class="lede">
    If you searched for a free online speed reader without creating an account, you want something that works in the tab you already have: paste text, open a PDF, flash words, and optionally hear them. That is the default BriskRead workflow.
  </p>

  <h2>What is a free online speed reader?</h2>
  <p>
    A free online speed reader is a website that helps you finish text faster using paced display — often <a href="/blog/rsvp-reading-explained">RSVP</a> (one word at a fixed point), bionic bolding, or a moving focus highlight — without installing desktop software. The best free tools also respect privacy and let you slow down when comprehension matters.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use BriskRead without signing up</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the <a href="/#importer-card">homepage importer</a>.</li>
    <li>Paste text, upload PDF/EPUB/TXT, run image OCR, or extract a public URL.</li>
    <li>Press Start — Flash (RSVP) is the default mode.</li>
    <li>Set WPM, press Space to play/pause, enable Audio Sync if you want dual-channel speech.</li>
    <li>Switch to Focus, Bionic, or Page when the material gets dense.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Step-by-step mode differences: <a href="/how-it-works">How BriskRead works</a>. Dedicated RSVP landing: <a href="/rsvp-reader">RSVP reader online</a>. Want a PDF read aloud instead? See <a href="/pdf-to-speech">PDF to speech</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What is free in BriskRead</h2>
  <table class="compare-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Feature</th><th>BriskRead (free)</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Signup required</td><td>No — optional account adds cross-device sync</td></tr>
      <tr><td>RSVP / Focus / Bionic / Page</td><td>Yes, all modes</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Audio Sync (browser TTS)</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Local PDF / EPUB / OCR</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Document length</td><td>Unlimited</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Library &amp; read-later queue</td><td>Unlimited</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Price</td><td>$0 — supported by ads</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>What it works well for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Newsletters, blogs, and familiar topics</li>
    <li>Full books and long reports — no length cap applies</li>
    <li>Trying RSVP or bionic reading on your own text</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Every feature is free, with no tiers. See also <a href="/blog/best-online-speed-readers">best online speed readers in 2026</a> and <a href="/blog/free-speechify-alternatives">free Speechify alternatives</a>.
  </p>

  <p class="blog-cta">
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/#importer-card">Open free speed reader</a>
    <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/reading-speed-test">Take a reading speed test</a>
  </p>
</BlogPost>
